<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Pt0.A3.T8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A3.T8.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Metrics of the selected clusterings for all datasets (top) and listing of all clusterings for DocVQA (bottom), where we used <span id="Pt0.A3.T8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">combined</span> embeddings and <math id="Pt0.A3.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=10</annotation></semantics></math> for our experiments.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Pt0.A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We select the optimal clustering <math id="Pt0.A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> by maximizing a heuristic quality score:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})=\arg\max_{\mathcal{E},\kappa}\left[S(C_{\mathcal{E},\kappa})+H(C_{\mathcal{E},\kappa})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})=\arg\max_{\mathcal{E},\kappa}\left[S(C_{\mathcal{E},\kappa})+H(C_{\mathcal{E},\kappa})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(C)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(C)</annotation></semantics></math> is the silhouette score <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite> measuring cluster compactness and <math id="Pt0.A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(C)=-\sum_{c=1}^{K}p_{c}\log p_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(C)=-\sum_{c=1}^{K}p_{c}\log p_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized entropy measuring cluster balance (where <math id="Pt0.A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a cluster’s proportion of the samples).
This heuristic prioritizes clusterings with both high internal coherence and balanced cluster sizes, which aligns with our manual inspection showing that such configurations produce semantically meaningful, interpretable document groupings suitable for seed selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Configurations <math id="Pt0.A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> are ranked using cumulative position scores: on each dataset,
the top <math id="Pt0.A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> configurations receive points from <math id="Pt0.A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> down to 1 based on their
composite metric ranking. Final rankings aggregate these scores across all
datasets as <math id="Pt0.A3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(\mathcal{E},\kappa)=\sum_{d}r_{d}(\mathcal{E},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>d</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(\mathcal{E},\kappa)=\sum_{d}r_{d}(\mathcal{E},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> and are listed in <a href="#Pt0.A3.T7" title="In Appendix 0.C Embeddings and Clustering ‣ DocDjinn: Controllable Synthetic Document Generation with VLMs and Handwriting Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.
Based on these rankings and manual inspection we select a clustering configuration <math id="Pt0.A3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{E}^{*},\kappa^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> for each dataset.
Metrics for the selected configurations and metrics for all configurations on DocVQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite> are shown in <a href="#Pt0.A3.T8" title="In Appendix 0.C Embeddings and Clustering ‣ DocDjinn: Controllable Synthetic Document Generation with VLMs and Handwriting Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, with the corresponding clusters visualized in <a href="#Pt0.A3.F4" title="In Appendix 0.C Embeddings and Clustering ‣ DocDjinn: Controllable Synthetic Document Generation with VLMs and Handwriting Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and <a href="#Pt0.A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix 0.C Embeddings and Clustering ‣ DocDjinn: Controllable Synthetic Document Generation with VLMs and Handwriting Diffusion" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.21824v1/cord_scatter_embedding_src=combined_min_cluster_size=10_nclusters=22.svg" id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">CORD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, <span id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">combined</span>, <math id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=10</annotation></semantics></math>, 22 Clusters</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.21824v1/doclaynet_4k_scatter_embedding_src=combined_min_cluster_size=10_nclusters=48.png" id="Pt0.A3.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/340;" width="476" height="340" alt="Refer to caption">
